sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-18: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.53";
    dc:description "The age contrast in proportions is directly measurable and would clearly confirm or refute the claim for these three domesticated species. The obstacle is data organization: published growth series would have to be compiled study by study, and they cover some dog and horse breeds far better than a balanced sample of pigeon breeds. That is a restricted, paper-by-paper test rather than an analysis of an existing public dataset.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For dog, horse and pigeon breeds, compare multivariate distances among breeds at neonatal or juvenile stages and at adulthood on the same landmarks, excluding or separately noting early-appearing exceptions such as the short-faced tumbler. The claim is confirmed if among-breed distance increases with age for the breed-diagnostic proportions, and refuted if neonates already differ as much as adults across those breeds.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Age-by-breed measurements exist as scattered veterinary and pigeon studies, not as one open morphometric table.", "Body size and allometry change proportions within a breed as it grows, and must be separated from true among-breed divergence.", "Breed standards and show data describe adults, so the juvenile half has to be recovered from separate growth papers.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.58"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.533"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of darwin1859-ch13-18 by Grok 4.7: 0.35";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.35"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok>.
